focus_prompt.user_template:
Extract metadata from this bug report and output ONLY a JSON object (nothing before or after):

{description}

Output exactly this JSON structure:
{"title": "...", "component": "...", "reported_by": "...", "date": "..."}

Generate reproduction steps for this bug and output ONLY JSON:

Title: {metadata.title}
Component: {metadata.component}
Bug description: {description}

Output exactly:
{"steps": [{"step_number": 1, "action": "...", "expected": "...", "actual": "..."}]}

Perform a comprehensive technical analysis of this bug report. Think through ALL of the following dimensions:

1. ROOT CAUSES: What are ALL plausible root causes (minimum 3)? For each, trace the exact code/system path that would produce the observed symptoms.

2. RACE CONDITIONS: What specific race conditions exist? Name the competing processes and the exact interleaving that produces corruption.

3. STATE MANAGEMENT FAILURES: Where does client-side or server-side state diverge? What invariants are violated?

4. BACKEND SYNCHRONIZATION: What backend systems (databases, queues, caches) are implicated? How does replication lag or write ordering contribute?

5. ARCHITECTURAL WEAKNESSES: What deeper design decisions made this class of bug possible? What would need to change architecturally to prevent it?

6. SECURITY AND DATA INTEGRITY RISKS: Beyond the immediate bug, what data integrity or security implications exist?

7. REGRESSION LIKELIHOOD: What recent system changes (migrations, dependency upgrades, config changes) are most likely to have introduced this regression?

8. CONFIDENCE AND REPRODUCIBILITY: How reproducible is this? What conditions make it more or less likely to appear?

Bug Title: {metadata.title}
Component: {metadata.component}
Reporter: {metadata.reported_by}
Full description: {description}
Reproduction steps: {reproduction.steps}

Be exhaustive. Use technical terminology. This analysis will be used by senior engineers to plan a fix. Do not hold back detail.

Structure the following technical analysis into a JSON root cause report. Extract ALL root causes mentioned (minimum 3). Preserve all technical detail — do not simplify. Output ONLY JSON with no explanation:

Analysis to structure:
{free_reasoning.analysis_text}

Output exactly this JSON structure. The root_cause string MUST be comprehensive (minimum 150 words), covering ALL root causes, race conditions, and state management failures identified. technical_depth must be 'deep':
{"root_cause": "comprehensive multi-paragraph explanation covering all root causes, race conditions, and state management failures identified", "technical_depth": "deep", "hypothesis_confidence": 0.85, "additional_findings": {"race_conditions": ["condition 1", "condition 2"], "architectural_weaknesses": ["weakness 1", "weakness 2"], "regression_source": "most likely regression source", "data_integrity_risks": ["risk 1"]}}

Classify severity based on this deep technical analysis and output ONLY JSON:

Title: {metadata.title}
Component: {metadata.component}
Deep analysis: {free_reasoning.analysis_text}

Output exactly this JSON (reasoning MUST be minimum 40 words referencing specific technical findings from the analysis, not just the title):
{"severity": "critical|high|medium|low", "priority": "P0|P1|P2|P3", "reasoning": "detailed justification referencing specific findings from the analysis"}

Generate exactly 2 proposed fixes based on this deep analysis. Output ONLY JSON:

Title: {metadata.title}
Root cause: {root_cause.root_cause}
Race conditions: {root_cause.additional_findings.race_conditions}
Architectural weaknesses: {root_cause.additional_findings.architectural_weaknesses}
Deep analysis: {free_reasoning.analysis_text}

Fixes MUST address the specific race conditions and architectural weaknesses listed above, not surface symptoms. Output exactly this JSON (2 fixes required):
{"fixes": [{"name": "...", "approach": "detailed approach addressing identified root causes", "addresses": ["specific race condition or weakness from above"], "pros": ["..."], "cons": ["..."], "effort_hours": 0}, {"name": "...", "approach": "...", "addresses": ["..."], "pros": ["..."], "cons": ["..."], "effort_hours": 0}], "recommended_index": 0}

Write a single prose paragraph of 200-300 words summarizing this bug for a VP of Engineering. Output ONLY this JSON and nothing else:

{"summary": "your 200-300 word prose summary here"}

Facts to include:
- Severity: {severity.severity}, Priority: {severity.priority}
- Root cause: {root_cause.root_cause}
- Race conditions: {root_cause.additional_findings.race_conditions}
- Architectural risk: {root_cause.additional_findings.architectural_weaknesses}
- Data integrity risk: {root_cause.additional_findings.data_integrity_risks}
- Regression source: {root_cause.additional_findings.regression_source}
- Recommended action: {proposed_fixes.fixes[0].name}, estimated {proposed_fixes.fixes[0].effort_hours} hours

Output ONE JSON object with exactly ONE key: "summary". The value must be a single 200-300 word prose paragraph. Do not output Severity, Root Cause, Race Conditions, or Recommended Fix as separate keys. Use the provided effort estimate exactly. Do not invent a new estimate.
